{"y":1980,"label":"1979–80","coach":"Dom Perno","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":20,"l":9,"cw":3,"cl":3,"confFinish":"4th in Big East","finish":"nit","srs":3.37,"sos":-1.2,"ppg":74.6,"oppg":69.9,"story":{"headline":"Charter Members of the New Big East","text":"In 1979–80 UConn played its first season in the Big East Conference as one of the league's seven charter members, alongside Boston College, Georgetown, Providence, St. John's, Seton Hall and Syracuse. The Huskies' first league game was an 89–73 win over Seton Hall on December 22, 1979, and they went 3–3 in the six-game conference schedule. Sophomores Mike McKay (16.7 points) and Corny Thompson (15.8 points, 9.3 rebounds) led the way, with junior guard Bobby Dulin (11.3 points) and senior forward Jim Abromaitis, while Kentucky transfer Chuck Aleksinas sat out the year. A 73–66 loss at Utah in the Utah Classic became a UConn win when Utah forfeited for using an ineligible player, making the final record 20–9. At the first Big East tournament, in Providence, the Huskies beat Boston College 79–68 in the quarterfinals before top-seeded Syracuse routed them 92–61 in the semifinals. UConn then hosted St. Peter's in the first round of the NIT at the Field House in Storrs and lost, 71–56. Thompson made second-team All-Big East, McKay third team, and freshman Bruce Kuczenski the all-freshman team.","moments":[{"date":"1979-12-22","title":"First Big East game","text":"UConn beats Seton Hall 89–73 in its first game as a member of the Big East Conference."},{"date":"1980-02-28","title":"First Big East tournament win","text":"UConn beats Boston College 79–68 in the quarterfinals of the first Big East tournament at the Providence Civic Center."},{"date":"1980-03-05","title":"NIT First Round: L vs St. Peter's","text":"St. Peter's beats UConn 71–56 in the first round of the NIT at the Field House in Storrs."}],"honors":["Corny Thompson – Second-team All-Big East","Mike McKay – Third-team All-Big East","Bruce Kuczenski – Big East All-Freshman team"],"sources":["https://uconnhuskies.com/documents/download/2026/8/13/RECORD_BOOK_26-27_V2_.pdf","https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/schools/connecticut/men/1980-schedule.html","https://web.archive.org/web/20110924084118/http://www.bigeast.org/AbouttheBIGEAST.aspx","https://www.wildcatworld.com/player/chuck-aleksinas/"]},"roster":[{"pid":"mike-mckay-1","name":"Mike McKay","num":"5","cls":"SO","pos":"G","ht":"6-5","wt":190,"home":"Bridgeport, CT","pg":{"g":29,"gs":29,"mp":34.1,"pts":16.7,"trb":5.3,"ast":2.3,"stl":0.9,"blk":null,"tov":null,"fg_pct":0.473,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.742,"orb":null,"pf":2.7},"tot":{"mp":989,"fg":183,"fga":387,"fg3":null,"fg3a":null,"ft":118,"fta":159,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":153,"ast":67,"stl":25,"blk":null,"tov":null,"pf":77,"pts":484,"g":29},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.523,"efg_pct":null,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":null,"ws_per_40":null,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"corny-thompson-1","name":"Corny Thompson","num":"52","cls":"SO","pos":"F","ht":"6-8","wt":225,"home":"Middletown, CT","pg":{"g":29,"gs":28,"mp":34.2,"pts":15.8,"trb":9.3,"ast":2.4,"stl":1.6,"blk":null,"tov":null,"fg_pct":0.5,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.794,"orb":null,"pf":3.7},"tot":{"mp":993,"fg":167,"fga":334,"fg3":null,"fg3a":null,"ft":123,"fta":155,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":270,"ast":71,"stl":45,"blk":null,"tov":null,"pf":108,"pts":457,"g":29},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.561,"efg_pct":null,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":null,"ws_per_40":null,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"bobby-dulin-1","name":"Bobby Dulin","num":"15","cls":"JR","pos":"G","ht":"5-11","wt":175,"home":"Milford, CT","hs":"Foran (CT)","pg":{"g":29,"gs":29,"mp":32.3,"pts":11.3,"trb":1.7,"ast":4.3,"stl":2.9,"blk":null,"tov":null,"fg_pct":0.523,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.75,"orb":null,"pf":2.9}